# Anthropology Manifest

Codex references these sources to model human social evolution, tribal logic, belief systems, and material culture drift. These guide faction logic, language spread, relic evolution, and behavioral AI stances.

---

## 🏕️ Tribal Societies & Tool Use

**Name:** Human Origins – Smithsonian Institution\
**Type:** Public Museum Archive\
**URL:** https://humanorigins.si.edu/

Use: Fire use, early weapons, group logic, scavenger AI. Used for pre-tech races, nomadic bands, and prehistory worldgen.

---

## 🗣️ Linguistic Drift & Oral History

**Name:** Ethnologue Language Family Trees\
**Type:** Linguistic Atlas\
**URL:** https://www.ethnologue.com/browse/families

Use: Regional word mutations, language fracture, symbolic inheritance. Used for ancient dialects, faction translation, cryptic text.

---

## 🔥 Ritual, Burial, and Kinship Logic

**Name:** Cultural Anthropology – MIT OCW\
**Type:** OpenAccess Course Material\
**URL:** https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/anthropology/21a-00-introduction-to-anthropology-fall-2011/

Use: Ancestor rites, death logic, sacred object value. Powers necropolis design, heirloom systems, and spiritual dialogue triggers.

